Subject: Cantor Transportable Semantic State Compilation

Description: The compact, signed, provider-independent semantic representation through which Cantor transports a governed point of attention and reconstructs an operationally equivalent inference state without transporting hidden activations or provider-private caches.

& [SemanticContinuityIdentity] is the governing Cantor continuity decision
  + [specification_uuid] is aa2e75ed-5aa2-4dc6-b2e2-a752704e6163
  + [transported_subject] is articulated semantic state
  + [non_subject] is transformer hidden state, KV cache, sampling state, private chain of thought, or byte-identical provider context
  + [continuity_target] is resolute semantic reconstruction sufficient to preserve the intended purpose, distinctions, constraints, evidence balance, uncertainty, and next valid operations
  = conclusion: Cantor coordinates inference by recreating meaning, not by preserving neural computation

& [TransportableSemanticState] is the canonical portable attention state
  + [state_uuid] is stable state identity
  + [fabric_digest] is the exact admitted SOP semantic fabric version
  + [purpose_binding] is intended use, completion condition, and non-goals
  + [subject_binding] is focused identity, aliases, context boundary, and disjoint identities
  + [ordered_anchor_set] is concise semantic addresses arranged by inferential function
  + [active_relation_set] is the typed association, dependency, qualification, contradiction, causal, temporal, authority, and execution paths presently material
  + [directive_program] is the ordered attention and inference operations to apply
  + [constraint_set] is requirements, prohibitions, permissions, guards, and budgets
  + [evidence_balance] is supporting evidence, counterevidence, provenance, confidence, and applicability
  + [unresolved_set] is ambiguity, unknown, disagreement, omission, and pending query state
  + [transition_position] is the last committed semantic move and permitted next operations
  + [projection_digest] is immutable identity of the ordered compact expression
  = must: be expandable through exact semantic addresses into governing definitions and proof
  = must: declare every material omission caused by projection limits

& [AnchorOrganizationGrammar] is the meaning-preserving organization of concise terms
  + [purpose_first] establishes what the state is for before associations are interpreted
  + [identity_second] binds the subject and exclusion boundaries
  + [governance_third] loads authority, constraints, security, and truth conditions before proposals
  + [evidence_fourth] presents material support and counterevidence in a non-deceptive balance
  + [relation_fifth] activates only the paths needed to traverse the current question
  + [operation_sixth] states the attention or inference transform presently permitted
  + [uncertainty_last] preserves unresolved items and stop, query, or reframe triggers
  = may: use a purpose-specific ordering when a signed DirectiveProgram proves equivalent or superior
  - never: optimize surface brevity by removing an identity boundary, hard constraint, material counterexample, uncertainty, or source address

& [SemanticQueryCompiler] is the optimizer from input and fabric to a concise executable semantic query
  + [step_1_resolve] binds terms to exact candidate semantic identities
  + [step_2_discriminate] selects anchors that distinguish intended identity from plausible wrong identities
  + [step_3_close] follows required dependencies, guards, and authority edges
  + [step_4_rank] orders anchors and paths by material information gain under purpose, consequence, and budget
  + [step_5_factor] replaces repeated meaning with stable addresses and shared higher-order clauses
  + [step_6_schedule] arranges definitions, constraints, evidence, relations, directives, and queries in causally useful order
  + [step_7_project] emits the minimum sufficient TransportableSemanticState
  + [step_8_prove] records selected, omitted, expanded, rejected, and budget-clipped material
  + [step_9_test] reconstructs the state and executes semantic equivalence probes
  = must: retain exact deterministic planning before optional learned plan proposals
  = must: make organization an inspectable query plan rather than an opaque prompt trick

& [ResolutionContract] is the measurable degree of semantic state recreation
  + [address_recovery] is required semantic addresses resolve to the same admitted units
  + [identity_preservation] is the intended subject and its exclusion boundaries remain stable
  + [purpose_preservation] is completion criteria and non-goals produce the same permissible result class
  + [constraint_preservation] is hard requirements, prohibitions, permissions, and stop conditions survive
  + [evidence_preservation] is material support, counterevidence, provenance, and uncertainty remain available
  + [operation_preservation] is permitted next semantic moves remain equivalent
  + [probe_equivalence] is a declared test set produces equivalent interpretations, admissions, rejections, and required queries
  + [provider_variance] is allowed difference in wording or non-material reasoning between consumers
  = must: specify thresholds by purpose and consequence class
  - never: claim reconstructed state is identical merely because its text or digest matches

& [SpeedAccuracyConvergence] is the conditional optimization principle
  + [shared_cause] is organization that removes irrelevant ambiguity and redundant expansion while preserving every material distinction
  + [speed_gain] is fewer candidates, paths, tokens, lookups, passes, and corrections
  + [accuracy_gain] is fewer wrong identities, missed guards, distracting neighbors, contradictory instructions, and context-placement failures
  + [sufficiency_envelope] is the range in which further concision preserves the ResolutionContract
  + [overcompression_fault] is any reduction that crosses the sufficiency envelope and loses material semantic state
  = conclusion: speed and accuracy can improve together when concision increases semantic density without reducing material coverage
  - never: presume the shortest expression is the most accurate

& [SemanticDensityObjective] is the query-plan scoring target
  + [maximize] is required-address recall, identity discrimination, constraint coverage, evidence balance, next-operation clarity, and proof recoverability
  + [minimize] is redundancy, irrelevant neighbors, unresolved aliasing, token cost, traversal cost, latency, and corrective reentry
  + [hard_floor] is complete preservation of non-waivable truth, security, authority, and consequence constraints
  + [comparison] is measured against verbose expansion, unordered anchors, keyword retrieval, and exact graph baseline
  = must: report accuracy and cost separately even when one organization improves both

& [CooperativeTransportCycle] is semantic-state exchange between inference participants
  + [step_1_compile] is Cantor compiles the current TransportableSemanticState
  + [step_2_transmit] is the state, fabric digest, and projection proof move to another provider or agent
  + [step_3_reconstruct] is the receiver expands required addresses and forms its local context
  + [step_4_probe] is Cantor verifies the ResolutionContract at the required consequence level
  + [step_5_infer] is the receiver proposes one or more attributed semantic moves
  + [step_6_admit] is Cantor resolves, validates, and commits or rejects those moves
  + [step_7_recompile] is Cantor emits the next compact state from the committed semantic position
  = must: treat local provider context as disposable and reconstructible
  = must: preserve a full authoritative record outside every compact projection

& [RequirementSet] is the traceable transportable-state collection
  + [TSS-001] is transport semantic meaning rather than neural runtime state
  + [TSS-002] is compile purpose, identity, anchors, relations, directives, constraints, evidence, uncertainty, and transition position into one portable state
  + [TSS-003] is organize concise terms through an inspectable purpose-sensitive query plan
  + [TSS-004] is measure reconstruction through semantic equivalence probes and consequence-scaled thresholds
  + [TSS-005] is optimize semantic density while preserving hard truth, security, authority, and evidence floors
  + [TSS-006] is distinguish joint speed-and-accuracy gains from unsafe overcompression
  + [TSS-007] is reconstruct disposable provider contexts from the durable semantic fabric and portable state

& [SJSProcessingTrace] is the transportable semantic-state justification record
  + [fold_1_subject] is provider-independent transport of anchored semantic meaning that reliably recreates a resolute inference state
  + [fold_2_boundary] is semantic continuity and organized query compilation inside; KV caches, hidden states, private reasoning, and identical neural replay outside
  + [fold_3_data_design] is state, fabric digest, purpose, subject, ordered anchor, active relation, directive, constraint, evidence, unresolved item, transition, query plan, projection proof, and equivalence probe
  + [fold_4_governance] is signed fabric binding, hard semantic floors, omission disclosure, consequence-scaled resolution, and no hidden authority
  + [fold_5_solution_shape] is resolve, discriminate, close, rank, factor, schedule, project, prove, reconstruct, probe, and recompile
  + [fold_6_fault_review] is unordered anchors, alias collision, omitted guards, deceptive concision, evidence imbalance, shortest-is-best error, provider wording conflation, and unrecoverable projection
  + [fold_7_phase_lock] is the semantic transport center is formed and may be proven through the existing bounded CoreAcceptance fixtures without latent-state or distributed-runtime expansion

